## What to do with these dreams

Keep the Dreaming workflow. It did the right thing: searched broadly, hydrated enough receipts to separate signal from noise, and stopped at review instead of mutating Brain, prompts, skills, or runtime packages.

The next work is not more report polish. It is ports and adapters: a leased memory adapter Cloudflare can call without importing Joel's private substrate.

Two ideas are not ready yet: dynamic workflow assembly and per-item review policy. They are probably right, but this run only found Typesense evidence for them. Keep them as candidates until another run hydrates better receipts.

