## Report node

The report template should be installed as a workflow node, not copied into each workflow as bespoke UI. The workflow asks for a human review surface; the package registry resolves a report renderer; the renderer turns typed artifacts into a SvelteKit/MDSvX static site; the Wzrrd adapter publishes only after the `wzrrd.site.publish` lease is approved.<MarginNote id="node-vs-adapter" number="2">The workflow node renders the review. The capability adapter publishes it. Conflating those is how template code turns into a secret-bearing side-effect surface.</MarginNote>

<PatternCards items={accessPatterns} label="System Dream findings" />

<h2 id="machine">Workflow state machine</h2>

This figure is rendered from the Dream run's pinned `workflow-plan.json` shape and redacted run facts. It is not claiming there was a generated XState machine artifact in this run. The artifact proves a workflow-plan state path and lane assembly; future reports should render the pinned generated XState machine when that artifact exists.

